WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:07.189
Hey, David, what is the best way to take advantage
of the Corona virus quarantine in terms of

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:10.219
personal development and how to use free time?

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:13.110
So I dealt with this a little bit on the Monday
bonus show.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.570
I've been trying to get back to number one.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:21.380
First of all, making sure that I don't get
out of, you know, exercise routines.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.890
And on nice days, I can run outside and bike.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:29.539
I'm working out inside of my place and trying
to keep that even without the gym as a place

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:31.710
that I normally would regularly go to.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.750
I think that's important.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.479
I've been reading a lot and trying to get
through a lot of books that normally would

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:37.580
take me longer to read.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.730
I have more time on weekends.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.180
I'm just sitting at home, so I'm just reading
books.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.309
I pulled out my painting supplies again, as
many of you remember from the New York City

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:46.830
days of the show.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.050
I used to do a little very, very bad amateur
painting.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.769
I'm back doing that a little bit more.

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:56.059
I'm trying to do projects around the house.

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:59.440
I've been watching a lot of courses on YouTube.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:05.050
Great philosophy, course of Rogue, a sort
of a refresher on mechanical physics, which

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.260
brought me back to my high school days.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.290
Anything that you believe, here's the way
I would sort of think about it.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:17.870
Consider this almost like a hibernation period
where instead of hibernating to reduce food

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:24.220
consumption, the way that bears would do during
the winter, your heart hibernating and trying

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:29.550
to improve yourself so that when we come out
of this thing someday, we don't know exactly

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:37.110
when you will come out a better, more prepared
person for getting back to normal life.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:41.900
And, you know, existing more vitally in society.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.960
And, you know, all of that's.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:44.960
I.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.680
Listen, we're all dealing with the same thing.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.840
That's the sort of best case scenario that
I can imagine.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:50.990
And that's what I'm trying to do.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.780
I will admit.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.270
I have been doing a little bit of videogaming,
former producer Lewis recommended some game

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.320
to me.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.760
I forget then it's some puzzle game that was
on.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.360
It was available on steam that he's been playing.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.400
I forget the name of it, but it's really,
really good.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.890
I've been playing that a little bit.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:14.540
I've been playing probably more online chess
than I normally do, but I think it's important

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.540
to mix things.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.310
I've been taking scheduled breaks from the
Corona virus news, as I did last Friday, Saturday

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.230
and most of Sunday.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.920
So I think it's about balance.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:30.819
Hanging out digitally and reconnecting with
friends is something that I've been doing.

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:36.520
And it's everybody is experiencing this this
feeling to some degree, unless you're not

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.520
doing anything.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.690
I know that in some states people are still
partying on beaches and going to concerts

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.690
and that sort of thing.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.319
But for those of us who are taking this seriously,
I get it.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:45.319
I'm here with you.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:49.031
We're doing a lot of livestreams to try to
give people opportunities to, you know, be

00:02:49.031 --> 00:02:50.360
in touch with us and participate.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:56.630
But those are some of my things try to come
out of this a more informed, more literate,

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.390
healthier person, if possible.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.140
And of course, meanwhile, trying to avoid
the virus itself.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.940
We've got a fantastic bonus show for you today.

